# A/B test readout: "Complete the set" recommendation widget

Copperleaf Cookware, product page test. Owner: ecommerce team.

## Setup

- Variant B adds the "Complete the set" recommendation widget (from our new personalisation platform) under the add-to-cart button on every product page. Control A is the current page.
- 50/50 split of all visitors, randomised per user.
- Primary metric: conversion rate = users who ordered / users exposed.
- Test window: 2026-09-14 to 2026-09-17.

## Sample ratio check

Control 36,236 users, treatment 36,265 users (49.98% / 50.02%). Chi-square 0.01, p = 0.91: no sample ratio mismatch.

## Results

| Variant | Users | Orders | Conversion rate | Revenue |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| A (control) | 36,236 | 1,177 | 3.25% | $104,159 |
| B (widget) | 36,265 | 1,308 | 3.61% | $114,848 |

**Conversion rate is up 0.36 points for B. Two-proportion z-test: z = 2.65, p = 0.008. The result is statistically significant at 95%.** 95% confidence interval for the difference: +0.09 to +0.62 points.

In plain terms, the widget makes about 0.4% more visitors buy.

The lift was consistent across the test, so we expect it to hold after launch.

## By device

| Device | A conversion | B conversion | Lift |
|---|---|---|---|
| Mobile | 2.90% | 3.35% | 15.5% |
| Desktop | 3.81% | 4.03% | 5.6% |

The widget clearly works on mobile and does little on desktop.

## Business case

The personalisation platform costs $65,000 per month (licence and support). Our gross margin is 40%. The test result is statistically significant, so the cost is justified.

## Recommendation

1. Ship the widget to 100% of mobile traffic on Monday and sign the 12-month platform contract.
2. Leave desktop on the current page for now.
DEVILS_ANALYST_EOF
